## Extract shared timed task-log renderer

Context: Task 3 of the Lakehouse build-progress plan requires moving the
existing Lakebase timed build-log renderer into a reusable Digital Twin frontend
component, while preserving Lakebase behavior and public wrappers. This prepares
Task 4 to reuse the same log component for Lakehouse without changing build
semantics.

Changes:

1. `tests/units/front/test_timed_build_log_contract.py`
   Added RED-first contracts for script load order, shared component wiring, and generic CSS scoping.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/timed-task-log.js`
   Extracted the full timed task-log renderer with `TimedTaskLog.create(config)` and `show/hide/render/export` instance methods.
3. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sync.js`
   Replaced Lakebase inline build-log implementation with wrapper delegation to a configured `TimedTaskLog` instance.
4. `src/front/static/query/css/query-sync.css`
   Re-scoped build-log styles from `#syncBuildLogCard` to the shared `.timed-task-log-card` class.
5. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sync.html`
   Added `.timed-task-log-card` to the Lakebase build-log card without changing IDs or markup structure.
6. `src/front/templates/dtwin.html`
   Loaded `query/js/timed-task-log.js` before `query-databricks-build.js` and `query-sync.js`.

